  "title": "Ball bearings fatigue — lognormal",
  "title_pt": "Fadiga de rolamentos — lognormal",
  "note": "The 23 bearings again with a lognormal likelihood (maximum likelihood: mu 4.15, sigma 0.52). The two models agree in the middle of the data and disagree in the early tail: R(25 Mrev) is about 0.95 here against 0.91 with the Weibull, and B10 about 31 against 27 Mrev. The choice of model matters most where the data are thinnest.",
  "note_pt": "Os 23 rolamentos com verossimilhança lognormal (máxima verossimilhança: mu 4,15, sigma 0,52). Os dois modelos concordam no meio dos dados e discordam na cauda inicial: R(25 Mrev) dá cerca de 0,95 aqui contra 0,91 com a Weibull, e a B10 cerca de 31 contra 27 Mrev. A escolha do modelo pesa mais onde os dados são mais escassos.",
  "source": "Lieblein, J. and Zelen, M. (1956). Statistical investigation of the fatigue life of deep-groove ball bearings. Journal of Research of the National Bureau of Standards 57(5), 273-316. Also in Lawless (2003), Statistical Models and Methods for Lifetime Data, 2nd ed., Wiley.",
